From 79aeafff4ef2398d0f9b0d49ca32530d490b7d74 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:15:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] feat(client): selection brackets, refusal cues, and
 rejection text (M9.1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two presentation gaps the human pass surfaced:

- Selection was invisible: the brightened team color alone does not
  read as "selected" at play distance. selection_quads() draws four
  corner brackets around each selected entity's projected position —
  the persistent read the player can trust.

- Rejected orders were silent: the plan's command gate refuses bad
  orders by design (fog-hidden targets, wrong capability, unaffordable
  costs), and the client dropped those events on the floor — which
  reads on screen as "the controls don't work". FeedbackState::refuse()
  now records the refusal at the order's click point (a fading red
  square, refusal_quads) plus a HUD notice line with the reason
  (rejection_text maps every RejectReason to player-facing text; the
  match is total, so a new variant cannot ship silently).

Both are pure geometry over the snapshot + camera, unit-tested like
the rest of the module; refusals_seen joins the smoke summary's
evidence counters.
---
