 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20plan=20=C2=A711.3's=20controls,=20working=20(M9.1)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The DEBT-008 human pass on the M9 build: "nothing is moving, the
controls are bad, D goes left and A goes right, I can't move with the
mouse, I can't order my army to move or attack, nothing appears".
Root causes, all client-side:

- W/S signs now match the fixed camera axes (W pans up-screen).
- Pan speed is scaled by the real frame delta (34 tiles/s, clamped) —
  the old fixed per-frame speed made pan a property of the monitor's
  refresh rate. The arrow keys alias WASD.
- Mouse: wheel up zooms IN toward the cursor (zoom_toward keeps the
  cursor's ground anchor under the cursor; the direction was
  inverted), middle-drag grabs the ground and pulls it (pan_world),
  and edge scrolling pans when the cursor rests on a window border
  (focused windows only) — plan §11.3's "pan by edge + keys" had
  never landed, so the mouse could not move the camera at all.
- Right-click resolves context per §11.3 (orders::resolve_context_order):
  an enemy under the cursor orders Attack (previously IMPOSSIBLE — the
  client could not order an attack at all), a resource node orders
  Gather for the selection's workers, open ground orders Move. The
  command gate stays the sole authority; refusals surface as the new
  feedback cues.
- 'A' arms attack-move and the next left-click places it (the HUD
  shows the armed line; Esc/right-click cancels) — firing on key-down
  fought the key's camera-pan role. Key repeats no longer re-fire
  hotkeys (holding S spammed Stop orders through every OS repeat).
- The camera opens focused on the player's start at 26 tiles (the old
  map-center default at 58 tiles rendered the starting force as specks
  — "nothing appears on the screen") and re-frames on restart.
- frames_presented advances on every presented frame, not only in the
  --frames verification mode — in normal play it was pinned at zero,
  so M9's flashes and pings never expired and accumulated forever.
- The end screen centers in the actual viewport, not a guessed 320x240.

Verified end to end under Xvfb + llvmpipe with XTEST injection: 900
frames presented, drag-box selection of the 5 start entities, 2
commands submitted (context Move + armed attack-move), the loop
healthy through pan/zoom/middle-drag (the DEBT-008 recipe, extended).
